Feature: Data Validation and Processing for Sample Sales Data

  Background:
    Given a CSV file "sample_sales_data.csv" with columns "country_cd", "product_id", "qty_sold", "sales_date"
    And the schema used is "purgo_playground"

  Scenario: Validate and Process Happy Path Data
    Given the CSV file is successfully uploaded to the system
    When the data is processed
    Then the data should be stored in "purgo_playground.sales_data" table
    And each entry should have a valid "country_cd", "product_id", "qty_sold", and "sales_date"
    And "qty_sold" should be a positive integer
    And "sales_date" should be in "YYYY-MM-DD" format
    
  Scenario: Handle Invalid Quantity Data
    Given a CSV file contains "qty_sold" data that is not a positive integer
    When the data is processed
    Then an error message "Invalid quantity for product_id at sales_date. Quantity must be a positive integer." should be logged

  Scenario: Handle Invalid Date Format
    Given a CSV file contains "sales_date" data not in "YYYY-MM-DD" format
    When the data is processed
    Then an error message "Invalid date format for product_id at sales_date. Date must be in YYYY-MM-DD format." should be logged

  Scenario Outline: Process and Validate Different Country Codes
    Given a "sample_sales_data.csv" file is provided
    When the data is processed
    Then entries with country code "<country_cd>" should be validated against the list of allowed country codes
    Examples:
      | country_cd |
      | US         |
      | CA         |
      | UK         |
      | IN         |
      | AU         |

  Scenario: Handle Data Integration with External Systems
    Given the data is stored in "purgo_playground.sales_data" table
    When the system integrates with external CRM for sales analysis
    Then the integration should use API endpoint "https://api.externalcrm.com/salesdata"
    And the data should be transmitted securely using TLS encryption
    And only fields "country_cd", "product_id", "qty_sold", "sales_date" are shared

  Scenario: Ensure Data Security and Compliance
    Given the schema "purgo_playground" has access control lists configured
    When data is accessed
    Then only users with "data_viewer" roles are permitted to access the data
    And all data access is logged with a timestamp and user ID

  Scenario: Validate Against Security and Compliance Standards
    Given data is stored and processed in "purgo_playground"
    When validation occurs
    Then the system should comply with GDPR requirements for data handling
    And log a message "Data processing and storage complies with GDPR" on successful validation
